			"type": "text",
			"text": "Afrocascudo is a ray finned fish from Kemkem Formation of Morocco, dating back to the Late Cretaceous. Its name is mix of 'Afro' meaning africa and 'Cascudo' a portuguese term for some armored catfishes. It was a relatively small fish being 7.4 centimeters long. The order Afrocascudo belongs to is highly debated, with it thought to be either a catfish or a lepisosteiform (a group whose only extant members are gar)."
